  ## Goal 3 — Admin: manage events + room occupants (multiple workers per room)

  ### Schema change — IMPORTANT
  Current `RoomDoc.occupantId` is a **single** string. Switch to a list to support "add/remove worker in room 305" with
  multiple staff:

  ```dart
  // lib/data/models/room.dart
  final List<String> occupantIds; // was: String? occupantId
  ```

  Migrate existing docs in `scripts/migrate_room_occupants.dart`: `occupantIds = occupantId != null ? [occupantId] :
  []`. Keep reading legacy `occupantId` once, write new shape.

  `Person.roomId` stays as the canonical home room (a person lives in one primary room) — but a room can host many
  people. Reverse lookup is via `where('roomId', isEqualTo: roomId)` plus the room's `occupantIds` list (denormalized
  for fast room-detail reads). When admin adds/removes a worker, write **both** sides in a Firestore batch.

  ### Admin: Room detail page (`lib/admin/pages/admin_rooms_page.dart` → add detail route)
  - Room header: number, floor, type, Mongolian name (editable)
  - **Occupants section**:
    - List of current occupants with photo + name + role + remove button
    - "Add worker" → searchable picker over `people` collection, filtered by buildingId, excluding current occupants
    - Removing detaches both sides (room.occupantIds and person.roomId if it equals this room)
  - Save uses `WriteBatch` so room + person stay in sync.

  ### Admin: Events (`lib/admin/pages/admin_events_page.dart`)
  Full CRUD already partially exists — make sure it covers:
  - Create / edit / delete `CampusEvent`
  - Fields: title, description, building, floor, room (optional), start, end, category (career-fair / pitch / lecture /
  workshop / general)
  - "Pin to home" toggle → sets `featured: true`; home "Happening here" reads featured + active first.
  - On create, send an FCM topic message to `building_{buildingId}` so followers get notified. Admin app subscribes
  nothing; client app subscribes to topics for buildings the user follows.

  ### Security rules (`firebase/firestore.rules`)
  - `buildings`, `floors`, `rooms`, `people`, `events` — public read
  - Writes only if `request.auth.token.admin == true` (set the custom claim manually via Firebase Admin SDK once; or
  simpler: keep an `admins/{uid}` doc and gate writes on
  `exists(/databases/$(database)/documents/admins/$(request.auth.uid))`)
  - `users/{uid}` — read/write only by self; admin can read all

  ### Admin role
  Reuse existing `lib/admin/main_admin.dart` entry. Build admin as Flutter web (`flutter build web -t
  lib/admin/main_admin.dart`) and deploy to Firebase Hosting. End users get the mobile app; staff get the web admin URL.

